# Code owners
#
# Every path here has one owner today. That is the honest state of the project,
# not an aspiration -- listing a team that does not exist would mean reviews go
# to nobody and merge unreviewed.
#
# GitHub uses the LAST matching pattern, so the specific entries below override
# the catch-all above them.

* @Hari-builds-ideas

# The invariants. A change under these paths is the kind that looks fine in
# review and breaks tenant isolation, RBAC, audit immutability or feedback
# anonymity -- see SECURITY.md. They are called out separately so that when a
# second reviewer exists, these are the paths they get added to first.
/apps/tenancy/    @Hari-builds-ideas
/apps/rbac/       @Hari-builds-ideas
/apps/audit/      @Hari-builds-ideas
/apps/feedback/   @Hari-builds-ideas
/apps/identity/   @Hari-builds-ideas

# Deployment and data-handling surfaces: a mistake here is live before anyone
# reads the diff.
/config/settings/ @Hari-builds-ideas
/deploy/          @Hari-builds-ideas
/scripts/         @Hari-builds-ideas
/Caddyfile        @Hari-builds-ideas
/docker-compose.prod.yml @Hari-builds-ideas
/.github/         @Hari-builds-ideas
